  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024, the Mekong Safeguards Program (Mekong Safeguards), in collaboration with the Energy Policy and Planning Office and the Electricity Generating Authority of Thailand, supported the updating of Thailand&#x2019;s Power Development Plan to include socioeconomic and environmental considerations using the Low Emissions Analysis Platform/Next Energy Modelling system for Optimisation model. The Planning Office proposed updated indicators to Thailand&#x2019;s Minister of Energy and presented the revised Power Development Plan at public hearing events in May 2024. At the same time, Mekong Safeguards worked with multiple companies to address gaps in their environmental, social and governance (ESG) policies and practices. With Mekong-Australia Partnership support, Thai power developer B.Grimm Power revised its Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) standards to improve policies on climate, water management, biodiversity, and stakeholder engagement. Wind energy developer, The Blue Circle strengthened its gender inclusive policies and practices while Vietnam&#x2019;s Saigon Asset Management developed a risk management tool to strengthen investment screening criteria and processes. Successful adoption of strong ESG standards by private sector developers and investors helps create best-practice case studies that can be replicated in other Mekong subregion projects.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Vietnam, the WE RISE Together program implemented by UN Women completed and disseminated a policy report which highlighted key findings from gender responsive procurement stakeholder mapping, a study on the legislative landscape, and capacity assessments. The Mekong-Australia Partnership supported the development of two handbooks on women SMEs access to state supporting policies and their participation in domestic and international markets through e-commerce. These reports were finalised in October 2024. The project worked in collaboration with Thailand&#x2019;s Office of Small and Medium Enterprises Promotion to develop an official definition of &#x2018;women-owned business&#x2019; that was approved by the SME Promotion Committee (chaired by the Prime Minister) in November 2024. The definition provides the foundation to support a national approach to collecting sex-disaggregated SME data to enable targeted policy development for women-owned businesses in Thailand. UN Women&#x2019;s 2024 Women&#x2019;s Empowerment Principles Awards ceremony in Thailand recognised 18 businesses for their efforts in advancing gender equality across value chains. Recognition tokens were offered to five Thai government departments which demonstrated a commitment to women&#x2019;s economic empowerment.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong Safeguards program supports strengthened environmental, social and corporate governance safeguards in infrastructure and energy development in the Mekong subregion, with a specific focus on impacts on women and vulnerable groups. During the reporting period, Mekong Safeguards undertook community outreach needs assessments and capability training for the communities, business owners and stakeholders affected by a high-speed railway development between Bangkok and Nakhon Ratchasima.  The program worked with the Thai Government to ensure that communities impacted by the project were consulted and able to mitigate against any negative impacts on households living in the path of the railway. It conducted outreach, focus groups and needs assessments with local stakeholders and ensured engagement by less represented groups including women-owned and run microbusinesses, people with hearing, visual and physical disabilities, and older aged persons. The work strengthened their resiliency to shocks caused by the railway development, including displacement and heightened flood-risk damage. It also empowered women-owned businesses by specifically training them to meet the requirements for government support to facilitate their access to new markets because of the high-speed railway development.
Through the WE RISE Together program, which promotes gender-responsive procurement in Thailand and Vietnam, succeeded in having both governments adopt policy mechanisms that target support for Women Owned Businesses to better engage in a supply chain. It also directly trained multiple women-owned businesses to prepare them to engage with other businesses while also engaging with companies to be more intentional towards inclusive procurement. A notable result was multiple businesses in Thailand pledging their commitments towards women&#x2019;s economic principles, including creating equal market opportunities for all.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WE RISE Together program, which promotes gender-responsive procurement (GRP) in Thailand and Vietnam, saw both national governments adopt policy mechanisms that target support for Women Owned Businesses (WOBs) to better engage in supply chains.  With the support of the program, the Thai Office of Small and Medium Enterprises Promotion (OSMEP) submitted the draft definition of WOBs to the Small and Medium Enterprises Promotion Committee (Chaired by the Prime Minister of Thailand) in November 2023. Once endorsed, an official definition will lay the base for a potential sex-disaggregated Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) database and will support the formulation and implementation of programs and policies targeting WOBs in Thailand at the national and provincial levels. In Vietnam, the Ministry of Finance adopted a new guidance that enables the targeting of technical advice and human resource development support to women-owned Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs), and SMEs that employ female workers.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
